      "file": "localization/english/ac/fab_ac_05_north_l_english.yml",
      "line": 50,
      "text": "fab_ac_north.0012.desc:0 \"The scream tears me from sleep before the horns begin. Beyond the inn, men flee from a mountain of wings and blood. [global_var:fab_north_slain_dragon.GetName] lies dead upon the riverbank, a white weirwood shaft buried in one great eye.\\n\\nBrandon Snow crossed the Trident beneath the moon, passed my sentries, and did what every king in Westeros deemed impossible. One of the three dragons who forged my victories will never fly again. Across the water the northmen roar his name, believing the spell of Valyria broken.\\n\\nTwo dragons remain, and two dragons are enough to melt the snows from Moat Cailin to the Wall. House Stark chose blood when I offered the knee. I shall answer in the words of my house.\""
    },
    {
      "file": "events/aegons_conquest/fab_ac_05_north.txt",
